{"id":"6635293aee21a51a635e22a2","slug":"rembrandt-van-rijn-canal-with-a-large-boat-and-a-bridge","title":"Canal with a Large Boat and a Bridge","artists":["Rembrandt van Rijn"],"date":"1650","medium":"Etching on paper","dimensions":"3 3/8 × 4 3/8 in","image":"aY3FZmj_iSmUeFMmMGwS7A","c":["#393026","#a28d71","#a38e77"],"said":[{"k":"note","q":"This superb etching, entitled Canal with a Large Boat and a Bridge, displays the artistry and detail for which Rembrandt's prints are renowned. This small and exquisite landscape is often understood to be the pendant of another small etching from the same year, Canal with an Angler and Two Swans(NH 253), based on their similar size, style and rounded platemark above.","by":"M.S. Rau, on Artsy"}],"events":[{"k":"made","y":"1650","q":"1650","o":1,"s":[0]},{"k":"owned","who":"Marsden Jasael Perry","q":"Marsden Jasael Perry, Providence, Rhode Island","ll":[41.824,-71.4128],"w":"Providence, US","p":"providence-us","pr":"city","o":1,"s":[1]},{"k":"sold","y":"1908-05-18","e":"1908-05-23","who":"H. G. Gutekunst","v":"H. G. Gutekunst","n":"lot 1304","q":"H. G. Gutekunst, Stuttgart, 18-23 May 1908, lot 1304","ll":[48.7784,9.18],"w":"Stuttgart, DE","p":"stuttgart-de","pr":"city","o":2,"s":[1]},{"k":"owned","who":"Private collection","q":"Private collection, United Kingdom","w":"GB","o":3,"s":[1]},{"k":"owned","who":"M.S. Rau","q":"M.S. Rau, New Orleans","ll":[29.9561,-90.0734],"w":"New Orleans, US","p":"new-orleans-us","pr":"city","o":5,"s":[1],"x":[0]},{"k":"written","who":"Bartsch, Adam","t":"Le Peintre graveur","pub":"Le Peintre graveur","pg":"Catalogue Number 236","q":"Bartsch, Adam. Catalogue Number 236. In Le Peintre graveur.","o":1,"s":[1]},{"k":"written","who":"Nowell, Usticke","n":"R+. A Scarce Landscape. Plate not in existence.","q":"Nowell, Usticke. R+. A Scarce Landscape. Plate not in existence.","o":2,"s":[1]},{"k":"written","t":"The New Hollstein Dutch","pub":"The New Hollstein Dutch","pg":"Catalogue Number 252","n":"The Se